    },
    "body": "Casey requires a discrete model path with no floating-point computation, including learning. Preserve the unfinished S1/S2 floating-point qualification and reviewed writer repair as inactive restoration material, record the actual observations and pod closure, and carry the SpiralCore/E8/FBS routing contract with Hamming as one factor. No active model implementation changes and no hold is released.\n\nLatest executed evidence is31/33 at49b6b2bf9; the final7569 writer repair built but its regression/replay remained NOT_RUN after the owner correction. The patch restores the exact full saved tree from pinned main base; source bundle and all CUDA receipts are in a round-trip-verified iCloud archive. The owned pod is deleted and fresh status reports zero running pods.\n\nValidation: isolated Git-index restoration reproduces tree312574e108b96e33d556fca9b7123711138d6799 exactly; source bundle verification passes; Rust D23/D25 ratchets pass1641/93; Rust shard integrity and all8state formats pass; non-archive diff whitespace passes; the byte-preserved patch retains three whitespace-only context lines. Independent review covered preserved outcomes, scope, restore hashes and owner-direction attribution. No numerical or model compute for this preservation delivery. The legacy Python claim-wording script was not run; claim wording reviewed directly under the owner Rust-only direction.\n\nLine: starling read, inactive preservation · prior count3/3 unchanged, not a mechanism negative or headline reset · headline unchanged. Training and separate M2 hold HELD.\n\nReferences #2032. References #2028.\n",
